        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0572" n="560" xml:id="pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6591: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-11T14:00:00+01:00">November 11,
                            1940—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1032. Regarding invasion of Greece: In opinion of Foreign Office, based on its
                    reports from Continent, it came to ears of Mussolini some weeks ago that Hitler
                    was offering French Morocco to Franco and at same time assuring Laval that no
                    further territorial concessions would be demanded of France. This so angered
                    Mussolini that since he had continuously received reports from his Minister at
                    Athens that Greeks would offer absolutely no resistance, he decided on immediate
                    invasion, expecting to face Hitler at their meeting in Florence with a <hi
                        rendition="#italic">fait accompli</hi>. Unlooked for stand of Greek Army and
                    people has for moment set Axis collaboration awry and much annoyed Hitler who
                    desired a <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi> in Balkans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
